Vitri — CNF preprocessing and vtree construction library
--------------------------------------------------------
Apache License 2.0. Full text: vendor/vitri/LICENSE (notices/vitri/LICENSE).

Pinned as the vendor/vitri submodule. Vitri vendors and builds CaDiCaL and the
Arjun stack (Arjun, CryptoMiniSat, cadiback, SBVA), and links FlowCutter
through the goatd crate. Their copyright notices, exact provenance, local
modifications and complete licence texts are maintained with that library:

  vendor/vitri/docs/THIRD-PARTY.md (notices/vitri/THIRD-PARTY.md)

That file links goatd's own THIRD-PARTY.md for the FlowCutter backend
(notices/vitri/goatd-THIRD-PARTY.md). Both are the authoritative attribution
for the native dependency stack.

Rust crates
-----------
The other dependencies are Rust crates that Cargo fetches from crates.io, each
under its own licence; Cargo.lock names every one and its version. One of them,
tikv-jemalloc-sys, builds the jemalloc allocator into the binary. jemalloc is
BSD-2-Clause: a binary distribution must reproduce its copyright notice, which
is the file jemalloc/COPYING inside that crate (notices/jemalloc/COPYING).
